course: dictionary
lesson: 7622
title: Probation: a trial time
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Probation has more than one meaning, so the context tells you which one is meant. «Probation at work is a trial period, often three or six months, when the worker and employer see if the job fits.» The clues are trial period and see if the job fits, so probation here means a test time at the start of a new job.
explain: Law is the other common use. A person who broke the law may stay out of prison, but must behave well and meet a probation officer for a set time. The clues are behave well and meet regularly. Ask yourself: what would fit here? A chance to change, not a prison sentence.
explain: Grown-ups «wait on probation in a new job, and later hope for a pay rise or a promotion.» Probation comes first, and the good things come after it. Swap in your meaning, a trial time, and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Probation means a trial time, a test period to see if something works out.
fact: «Probation» at work is a trial period at the start of a new job, often three or six months.
fact: In law, probation lets a person stay out of prison if they behave well and meet a probation officer.
fact: In some schools in the USA, academic probation is a warning for a student whose marks or behaviour are too poor.
fact: Useful phrases: on probation, probation officer, a probation period, break probation.
exercise: «Probation at work is a trial period, often three or six months.» What is probation at work? | *A trial period to see if the job fits | A prize for good workers | A kind of school exam | A holiday before you start work
exercise: A person on probation for breaking the law must behave well and meet a probation officer. What does the officer do? | A long journey to prison | Cooks dinner for the court | Writes new laws for the country | *Meets the person regularly to check their behaviour
exercise: Grown-ups «wait on probation in a new job». Which word is closest in meaning to probation here? | *Trial | Prize | Holiday | Promotion
test: Lina is on a probation period at her new job, which lasts three months. What does this tell you? | She has won a prize for good work | *Her employer is checking whether she suits the job | She has been sent to prison | She is a teacher on holiday
test: A student is put on academic probation when their marks are too poor. What does this mean? | A reward for top marks | A new subject to learn | *A warning that marks or behaviour must improve | A holiday from school
exam: Mo has been on probation for a year and must meet his probation officer each month. What does probation mean here? | A warning from the school | A trial job at a shop | *A set time of good behaviour under supervision | A journey to a new town
